{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00262","versions":[{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00262","release":"R19-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00262","release":"R20-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00262","release":"R21-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00262","release":"R22-11","text_captured":false,"meta":{"trigger_kind":"pdf_presence","source":"classic_upstream"}},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00262@rel:R23-11#10f5a91e","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_SecOC_00262","release":"R23-11","content":"[SWS_SecOC_00262]⌈\nFor a Tx Secured I-PDU with SecOCAuthPduHeaderLength > 0, the SecOC module\nshall add the Secured I-PDU Header to the Secured I-PDU with the length of the\nAuthentic I-PDU within the Secured I-PDU, to handle dynamic Authentic I-PDU.\nNote: Primary purpose of this Header is to indicate the position of Freshness Value and Authenticator\nin Secured I-PDUs with dynamic length Authentic I-PDU.Also some buses which cannot select\narbitrary length of L-PDU (e.g. CAN FD and FlexRay) require this Header, because the position of\nFreshness Value and Authenticator is not always at the end of the Secured I-PDU, as lower layer\nmodules (e.g. CanIf and FrIf) may add bus-specific padding bytes after processing at SecOC (then the\nL-PDU containing the Secured I-PDU with padding will be: Secured I-PDU = Secured I-PDU Header |\nAuthentic I-PDU | Freshness Value | Authenticator | Bus-specific padding).\n⌋(SRS_SecOC_00006)","meta":{"source_pdf":"SWS_SecureOnboardCommunication.pdf","source_page":40,"trigger_kind":"snippet_ingest"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-04T00:00:00+00:00","text_key":"f3eedd7df400","rejoin":{"rule":